Preserve the original signed-BYTE camera lane field at 0x77cf3a.

FUN_00428a8c tests the camera's lane against the last strip lane before
clamping it to the track wall. Original 0x429294 loads BYTE [0x77cf3a]
into AH; TEST AH,AH / JG at 0x42929d..0x42929f is a signed-byte test.
The right-wall branch loads DWORD [0x77cf37] at 0x42946f, then SAR EDX,24
at 0x42947a: this is the same field, sign-extended from BYTE 0x77cf3a.
Ghidra's int alias read three adjacent structure bytes as part of the lane.

Actual original L1 cf596/ticks1193 has bytes 03 ff 00 00 at 0x77cf3a.
Both ports' old alias read 65283 rather than lane 3, missing the original
right-wall clamp and camera bump (0x463ef0: original=32, port=0). Camera
x/z differ by 6/5 world units while car 4's physical position, input clock
and all calculated random states agree. The next presented image and seven
more at cf596..602 differ broadly. Read exactly the original signed byte;
the two camera uses have the same signed semantics as the proven loads.

